---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Radin Khayyam's research has two tracks: learning theory with Prof. Zafer Doğan at Koç University, and applications of AI in biomedical signals, recommender systems, and personalized AI."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Two tracks. Learning theory, with Prof. Zafer Doğan, is the work I am doing now. Applications of AI are the
      biomedical record and the personalized systems behind it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Learning theory</h2>
    <p>This is the primary track, and it is ongoing. I do not have a paper to point to yet.</p>
    <p>
      I started the MSc in artificial intelligence at Koç University in October 2026, on the Presidential Fellowship.
      The group is MLIP. The advisor is Prof. Zafer Doğan.
    </p>
    <p>Three questions organize the work.</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Generalization of machine learning models.</li>
      <li>
        Connecting classical learning theory to modern deep learning, including how models such as transformers behave
        and what an optimizer does to that behaviour.
      </li>
      <li>
        Learning from structured data that is closer to real-world data, rather than from idealized i.i.d. assumptions.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Applications of AI</h2>
    <p>
      The second track is applications. Two interests sit here, and neither is the whole of the site. One is
      recommender systems and personalized AI. The other is biomedical signal processing and AI in healthcare, which is
      where the EEG and brain-computer interface work belongs. The Solico Group systems are the recommender and
      language-model side of this track, and they are written up on <a href="/projects">Projects</a>.
    </p>

    <article class="repo">
      <div>
        <h3>ICBME 2024</h3>
        <p>
          Radin Khayyam and Mohammad B. Shamsollahi, “Comparison of Methods for Hand Trajectory Estimation in 3D Space
          Using EEG Signals”, 31st National and 9th International Iranian Conference on Biomedical Engineering (ICBME),
          2024.
        </p>
        <p class="link-row">
          <a href={site.paper}>Paper</a>
          <a href={site.slides}>Slides</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="when">2024</p>
    </article>

    <article class="repo">
      <div>
        <h3>BSc thesis</h3>
        <p>
          Hand trajectory estimation based on EEG signals, at Sharif University of Technology, with Prof. Mohammad B.
          Shamsollahi. I compared mLR, PLSR, KRR, MLP, and a Kalman filter with CNN, LSTM, and GRU models, to see which
          estimated hand position from EEG most effectively.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="when">September 2023 to August 2024</p>
    </article>

    <article class="repo">
      <div>
        <h3>University of British Columbia</h3>
        <p>
          Remote research internship with Prof. Sepideh Hajipour on advanced EEG denoising in multimodal neuroimaging. I
          worked on an algorithm to denoise EEG recorded at the same time as fMRI and brain stimulation (GVS).
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="when">August 2024 to January 2025</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Earlier research</h2>
    <article class="repo">
      <div>
        <h3>Chinese University of Hong Kong</h3>
        <p>
          In-person internship with Prof. Zhenyu Yan on device authentication using induced body electric potentials. I
          worked on an authentication system for IoT devices, implementing wireless protocols on ARM microcontrollers,
          including the CC2650, to transfer and process the measurements.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="when">July 2023 to September 2023</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
